+	config HZ_500
+		bool "500 HZ"
+	help
+	 500 Hz is a middle ground between 300 Hz and 1000 Hz — most of
+	 1000 Hz's finer scheduling/timer granularity (touch and audio
+	 latency) at meaningfully less timer-interrupt overhead than a
+	 full 1000 Hz. A common choice on mobile/Android kernels that
+	 don't want to pay the full 1000 Hz interrupt cost.
+
